  <!-- ================= 2. EDITORIAL PHILOSOPHY ================= -->
  <section class="vaidyam-philosophy-section" id="philosophy">
    <div class="page-width vaidyam-container">
      <div class="philosophy-masthead">
        <span class="philosophy-subtag">EDITORIAL PHILOSOPHY • SINCE 2003</span>
        <h2 class="philosophy-title">Bridging Classical Shastra with Contemporary Science</h2>
        <p class="philosophy-lead">
          Vaidyam addresses a fundamental need in integrative healthcare: providing practicing physicians and scholars with rigorous clinical casuistry without sacrificing the timeless depth of classical treatises.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="philosophy-tri-grid">
        <div class="philosophy-card">
          <span class="card-roman">01</span>
          <h3>Physician-Reviewed Rigour</h3>
          <p>Every paper, clinical case, and botanical analysis is evaluated by an active board of BAMS, MD, and PhD practitioners across premier Ayurvedic medical colleges.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="philosophy-card">
          <span class="card-roman">02</span>
          <h3>The Readometer Metric</h3>
          <p>Articles are graded across three clear tiers: Level 1 (Foundational &amp; Lifestyle), Level 2 (Applied Pharmacology &amp; Formulations), and Level 3 (Classical Sanskrit Shastra Textual Exegesis).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="philosophy-card">
          <span class="card-roman">03</span>
          <h3>CARE-Standard Casuistry</h3>
          <p>Moving beyond anecdotal claims to international CARE-guideline single-patient reports with audited laboratory parameters, Bristol Stool scores, and explicit dosage protocols.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

